A note on logging: To save all your commands, when you start working in PyMOL open a log (File → Log). This will record everything you type.

Note: Copy/paste the commands that follow “PyMOL>” 


Show sticks of residues within 5 angstroms of your selection (to show binding site residues):
PYMOL> show sticks, byres all within 5 of SELECTIONNAME


If you wanted to make the water molecule smaller, type:
PyMOL>alter active_water, vdw=0.5
PyMOL>rebuild


Command to create colorblind-friendly images (if you want the background black, change the first line to say “black” instead of “white”): PYMOL>
bg_color white
set antialias=1
set orthoscopic=1
set gamma=1.15
set cartoon_fancy_helices, 1
set cartoon_fancy_sheets, 1
set_color wred, [0.788,0.000,0.140]
set_color wblue, [0.31,0.506,0.686]
set_color wgold, [0.855,0.647,0.125]
set_color wgreen, [0.134,0.545,0.134]
set_color wgray, [0.800,0.800,0.800]
set_color wrose, [0.65,0.47,0.55]
set_color wpurple, [0.37,0.31,0.62]
set_color mpurple, [0.75,0.57,0.80]
set_color mpgrey, [0.73,0.68,0.82]
set ray_shadows, 0
set ray_trace_fog, 1


To color using the command line (you can also follow the commands below with SELECTIONNAME to apply it to just a particular named selection): PYMOL>
util.cbag        green
util.cbac        cyan
util.cbam        light magenta
util.cbay        yellow
util.cbas        salmon
util.cbaw        white/grey
util.cbab        slate
util.cbao        bright orange
util.cbap        purple
util.cbak        pink


To hide/show non-bonded entities, usually water.
hide nonbonded
show nonbonded


To set the transparency of different entities (transparency - all surfaces, cartoon_transparency - backbone, stick_transparency - ligand/sidechain). The value following the command is between 0-1: PYMOL>
set transparency, 0.5
set cartoon_transparency, 0.6
set stick_transparency, 0.4

To split the structures from a multi-ligand .sdf file (obj is the name of the loaded multi-state object, and the prefix is what you would like the split states to be called):
split_states obj, prefix=lig


